      en: "Šumperk, the 'Gateway to the Jeseníky Mountains,' has a rich and varied history. Founded in the Middle Ages by German colonists, the city prospered from mining and later the textile industry, earning it the nicknames 'Little Vienna' or 'Moravian Manchester.' A dark chapter in the city's history is the infamous witch trials in the latter half of the 17th century, led by the inquisitor Heinrich Boblig von Edelstadt. The historic center, with its magnificent town hall in the Saxon Renaissance style, testifies to its former wealth. Today, Šumperk is an administrative and cultural center for the region and an ideal base for hiking and skiing in the Jeseníky Mountains."
