      en: "Krnov, located in the Czech part of Silesia on the border with Poland, was once a wealthy ducal town. Its prosperity was based on cloth manufacturing and organ building, especially through the world-renowned Rieger-Kloss company. The historic center, with its chateau, neo-Gothic town hall, and well-preserved townhouses, bears witness to its former wealth. A unique technical monument is the Moorish-Byzantine style synagogue, which houses an original Rieger organ. The city is also known for the Kofola soft drink, which originated here. Surrounded by the foothills of the Jeseníky Mountains, Krnov also offers opportunities for local recreation."
